   "qtype": "mcq",
   "section": "Section A",
   "stem": "Let $d$ be the distance of the point of intersection of the lines $\\frac{x+6}{3}=\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{z+1}{1}$ and $\\frac{x-7}{4}=\\frac{y-9}{3}=\\frac{z-4}{2}$ from the point $(7, 8, 9)$. Then $d^{2}+6$ is equal to :",
