   "qtype": "mcq",
   "section": "Section A",
   "stem": "Let two straight lines drawn from the origin O intersect the line $3x + 4y = 12$ at the points P and Q such that $\\triangle OPQ$ is an isosceles triangle and $\\angle POQ = 90^\\circ$. If $l = OP^{2} + PQ^{2} + QO^{2}$, then the greatest integer less than or equal to $l$ is :",
